 
          <p>Our Lego Duplo blocks are in short supply meaning we&rsquo;ll have to get creative to assemble, build, and rebuild new things. <em>I want a house on wheels!</em> is by far the most popular request here. No problem, we can do that, only to do that, we&rsquo;ll have to demolish that other structure over there. No? <em>But little brother is playing with that!</em> No he isn&rsquo;t? <em>But I want a house on wheels!</em> How to defuse this situation?</p>
<p>By building a less conventional house on wheels, of course. Or by building a row boat and claiming it&rsquo;s also a house. Or by attaching a few farm tools on it and claiming it can also act as a tractor. That also works. <em>Hey, no! No brother you can&rsquo;t have my house!</em> Wait since when is that your house? I&rsquo;m working on your house give me a minute. Why don&rsquo;t you build something yourself? <em>No. I can&rsquo;t. You must.</em> Ok then. <em>No! Brother can&rsquo;t have my figures! That&rsquo;s not allowed! Isn&rsquo;t it dad?</em> Sigh. We have twenty figures. Even if we would have two hundred, I think I&rsquo;d hear the same complaints.</p>
<p>Here&rsquo;s your house slash thing. Happy now?</p>
